nq9|n|The conscious and permanent subject of all psychical experiences, whether held to be directly known or the product of reflective thought; -- opposed to non-ego.	a:7s2,61,3~7s2,61,3
nqv|a|Surpassing; extraordinary; distinguished (in a bad sense); -- formerly used with words importing a good quality, but now joined with words having a bad sense; as, an egregious rascal; an egregious ass; an egregious mistake.	j:puk,69,4;b8w,57,2~puk,69,4;b8w,57,2	e:1huf,71,3;1byh,41,8~1byh,41,8;1huf,71,3
